  "facts": [
    "Opened in 1973, the Eisenhower Tunnel became the world’s highest vehicular tunnel at 11,158 feet, a record it held until surpassed by later projects like China’s Fenghuoshan rail tunnel.",
    "Construction began March 15, 1968, but fault lines forced a contractor’s bankruptcy and three workers lost their lives, underscoring the mountain’s stubborn resistance to tunneling.",
    "A 2007 retrofit lifted the clearance from 13 ft 6 in to 13 ft 11 in, slashing overheight alarms by up to 80% and adding a weigh‑in‑motion speed calculator for trucks on the steep 7% grades."
